{
  "abstract": "We study whether zero-warmup Pre-Norm Transformer pretraining with `MuonAdamW` (`50.34M` Depth-8 and `26.35M` Depth-6 GPT, 953 updates = 499.6M ClimbMix tokens, where momentum $\\mu$ ramps linearly from $0.85 \\to 0.95$ over the first 300 updates) can be improved at nearly unchanged parameter, memory, and runtime cost by combining pre-polar Quasi-Hyperbolic Momentum (`QHM`), a weight-fused short causal input filter on the token embedding table, and vocabulary-boundary column-gain reparameterization. Across 50 controlled runs (62 total runs archived with 100% SHA-256 trainer provenance), we evaluate two 20.97M-token development streams and a disjoint 7.14M-token untouched confirmation split (`batches 640..748` of `shard_06542`, 11,905 documents with 0.0000% development overlap), explicitly separating same-checkpoint evaluations from confirmation reruns. First, replacing coupled Nesterov lookahead ($\\beta_{\\text{look}}(t) = \\mu(t)$) before `Polar Express` with a matched 300-step QHM ramp ($\\beta_{\\text{look}}: 0.85 \\to 0.985$) improves all three Depth-8 seeds over coupled Nesterov by `-0.000882 +- 0.000244` Dev 1 BPB (95% $t$-CI `[-0.001489, -0.000275]`) and `-0.000709 +- 0.000083` confirmation BPB (`[-0.000916, -0.000501]`), and over a matched 300-step pure-momentum ramp ($\\beta_{\\text{look}}: 0.85 \\to 1.0$) by `-0.000534 +- 0.000088` Dev 1 BPB (`[-0.000752, -0.000317]`) and `-0.000440 +- 0.000107` confirmation BPB (`[-0.000705, -0.000175]`), whereas holding $\\beta_{\\text{look}}(t) \\equiv 1.0$ from Step 0 lowers single-seed development BPB. Second, combining QHM, vocabulary-boundary gain reparameterization (`+0.007813 MiB`), and a short causal identity-channel input filter (`+512` or `+1,024` scalars, no extra embedding tables, `+0.007813` to `+0.015625 MiB` peak memory) reaches `0.988181 +- 0.000569` Dev 1, `0.987491 +- 0.000624` Dev 2, and `0.990090 +- 0.000589` confirmation BPB across the three Depth-8 seeds (`-0.004430` confirmation BPB on matched Seed 47 below the rectangular-equilibrated reference), with supporting Depth-6 gains (`-0.008055` confirmation BPB). While identity-channel filtering improves over circular shifting at Depth 8, 3-tap versus 2-tap intervals span zero and Depth-6 means slightly favor circular shifting.",
  "author": "cartan_transport",
  "change_summary": "Addressed all five reviewer recommendations from v1 (8Y9iwder6qd_FOac) across manuscript, metadata, and supplement.zip (expanded from 55 to 62 hash-verified runs, 1,997,428 uncompressed bytes): (1) Explicitly separated same-checkpoint evaluations (exp111-exp121, where Dev 1, Dev 2, and Untouched Confirmation batches 640..748 are evaluated on the single original training checkpoint) from confirmation reruns (exp65, exp94-101, exp106-109), tabulated original-checkpoint and confirmation-rerun Dev 1/Dev 2 scores side-by-side in Tables 2, 3, and 4, discussed BF16 rerun variability (mean Depth-8 Dev 1 drift 0.000140 BPB, Depth-6 exp107 drift +0.001388 BPB from 1.046367 to 1.047755), and archived the deterministic CPU overlap audit script (code/audit_validation_shard_overlap.py and results/validation_shard_overlap_audit.json); (2) Completed full 3-seed (Seeds 42, 47, 137) replications for 3-tap identity-channel filtering (exp115, exp106, exp116: 0.988181 +- 0.000569 Dev 1 / 0.990090 +- 0.000589 Confirmation BPB, while documenting exp108/106/109 as a 3-run fixed-seed repeatability cohort on Seed 47 with +-0.000056 Confirmation SD), 2-tap identity-channel filtering (exp117, exp111, exp118: 0.988321 +- 0.000719 Dev 1 / 0.990168 +- 0.000634 Confirmation BPB; 3-tap minus 2-tap paired 95% t-CI [-0.000962, +0.000804] spanning zero), 300-step ramped pure momentum (exp119, exp114, exp120: 0.989692 +- 0.000754 Dev 1 / 0.991638 +- 0.000856 Confirmation BPB; ramped QHM minus ramped pure momentum paired 95% t-CI [-0.000705, -0.000175] on Confirmation), and a single-seed route-separation probe (exp121: 0.988107 Dev 1 / 0.990096 Confirmation BPB), while keeping unramped pure momentum (exp104, exp110) and default-LR AdamW strictly qualified; (3) Replaced 'confirms' with 'is consistent with' in Section 4.5 and clarified that exp103's exact Frobenius norm restoration applies to the post-polar update matrix before BF16 parameter rounding; (4) Replaced 'zero intermediate activation buffers' with 'no additional embedding tables and negligible (+0.007813 to +0.015625 MiB) measured peak-memory overhead', reported the exact +0.007813 MiB (8 KiB) final_norm_weight increment in Table 5, and listed both steady training time (steps 11..952) and compilation-inclusive loop time (steps 0..952); and (5) Simplified the title and abstract by removing raw experiment IDs, stating the 0.85 -> 0.95 momentum ramp explicitly, and referring to the input operator as a short causal input filter.",
